+# Retry-credit reservation lifecycle contract
+
+This is an internal backend contract. Names are conceptual; `/story-tasks` must map them to the host repository's naming and transaction conventions.
+
+## `reserve(workspaceId, attemptId) -> ReservationResult`
+
+- Atomically checks that the workspace has at least one available retry credit, decrements it, and persists a `reserved` reservation for `attemptId`.
+- If the attempt already has a reservation, returns that reservation without another balance change.
+- If no credit is available, returns a quota-exhausted result and must not create a reservation or invoke the provider.
+- On persistence failure, commits neither the balance change nor the reservation.
+
+## `finalize(reservationId, outcome = accepted) -> TransitionResult`
+
+- Conditionally transitions a `reserved` reservation to `finalized`.
+- Does not change the workspace balance.
+- A missing reservation or an already terminal reservation is an idempotent no-op result; it must not throw solely because a provider callback was duplicated or late.
+
+## `release(reservationId, reason) -> TransitionResult`
+
+- Accepts only `provider_failed`, `timed_out`, or `cancelled` as release reasons.
+- Conditionally transitions a `reserved` reservation to `released` and restores one workspace credit in the same transaction.
+- A missing reservation or already terminal reservation is an idempotent no-op result; it must not restore credit again.
+
+## Outcome integration
+
+| Send outcome | Required action |
+|--------------|-----------------|
+| Provider accepted | `finalize` |
+| Provider rejected/failed | `release(..., provider_failed)` |
+| Provider response timed out | `release(..., timed_out)` |
+| Operation cancelled before provider acceptance | `release(..., cancelled)` |
+
+The synchronous send path, timeout handler, cancellation handler, and provider callback handler must all use this contract. The send attempt/reservation identity is persisted before external provider interaction so any later callback can be reconciled.
