+# S004 retry-credit data model
+
+## Workspace retry quota
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rules |
+|-------|---------|-------|
+| `workspace_id` | Workspace that owns the quota | Primary ownership key. |
+| `available_retry_credits` | Credits available for new provider send attempts | Non-negative integer. Changed only in the same transaction as a legal reservation transition. |
+
+## RetryCreditReservation
+
+One reservation represents the accounting lifecycle of exactly one reminder-provider send attempt.
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rules |
+|-------|---------|-------|
+| `reservation_id` | Stable idempotency key | Unique; derived from or uniquely associated with the persisted send attempt. |
+| `workspace_id` | Quota owner | Must match the workspace whose balance is changed. |
+| `attempt_id` | Reminder send attempt | Unique within the reservation ledger; prevents two charges for the same attempt. |
+| `state` | `reserved`, `finalized`, or `released` | Starts as `reserved`; terminal states never transition again. |
+| `created_at` | Reservation time | Recorded when credit is reserved. |
+| `terminal_at` | Finalization or release time | Null while reserved; set only by the first legal terminal transition. |
+| `terminal_reason` | Outcome that closed the reservation | `accepted`, `provider_failed`, `timed_out`, or `cancelled` for auditability. |
+
+## State transitions
+
+| From | Event | To | Balance effect |
+|------|-------|----|----------------|
+| no reservation | reserve succeeds with credit available | `reserved` | decrement by 1 |
+| `reserved` | provider accepted | `finalized` | none |
+| `reserved` | provider failed | `released` | increment by 1 |
+| `reserved` | timeout | `released` | increment by 1 |
+| `reserved` | cancellation | `released` | increment by 1 |
+| `finalized` or `released` | any repeated terminal event | unchanged | none |
+
+## Invariants
+
+1. `available_retry_credits >= 0` at every committed state.
+2. A send `attempt_id` has at most one reservation.
+3. A reservation changes from `reserved` to a terminal state at most once.
+4. Only a successful reserve decrements balance; only the first release increments it.
+5. Creating a reservation and decrementing balance commit or roll back together. Releasing a reservation and incrementing balance commit or roll back together.
